This directory is intentionally empty.

mounts/ holds assets bind-mounted into
containers. The mount itself is declared in
docker/docker-compose-token-nodes.yaml.

It is bind-mounted read-only OVER
  organizations/peerOrganizations/org1.example.com/msp/keystore
inside the owner container, to shadow the Fabric CA ADMIN private key that
otherwise ships inside the organizations/ tree.

The owner node needs organizations/ for its own Fabric identity
(users/User1@org1.example.com/msp) and for peer/orderer TLS roots, so the
tree as a whole cannot simply be unmounted - but the CA admin key inside it
is a full CA superuser credential that the owner has no business holding.
Shadowing that one directory removes it while leaving everything else intact.

See scripts/registerWalletRegistrar.sh for the narrow credential the owner
uses instead.
